YM2612: the DAC value without shifting a negative number

The DAC value is the byte written to register 0x2A, centred on 0x80 and
scaled by 128. It is scaled with a left shift, and the shift of a negative
number is undefined behaviour, which UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer stops the
program at:

  src/chips/gens/Ym2612.cpp:1787:43: runtime error: left shift of negative
  value -128

A multiplication says the same thing and is defined. The value stays within
an int: the byte gives -128 to 127, and the product -16384 to 16256. Both
places that work it out are changed.

This is ADLplug-Next's own patch, applied to the submodule by
cmake/Patches.cmake when CMake configures, and it goes away once the change is
upstream.

diff --git a/src/chips/gens/Ym2612.cpp b/src/chips/gens/Ym2612.cpp
index 4535e0d..51d1123 100644
--- a/src/chips/gens/Ym2612.cpp
+++ b/src/chips/gens/Ym2612.cpp
@@ -819,7 +819,7 @@ int Ym2612Private::YM_SET(int address, uint8_t data)
 
 		case 0x2A:
 			// Set the DAC value.
-			state.DACdata = ((int)data - 0x80) << 7;	// donnée du DAC
+			state.DACdata = ((int)data - 0x80) * 128;	// donnée du DAC
 			break;
 
 		case 0x2B:
@@ -1784,7 +1784,7 @@ int Ym2612::write(unsigned int address, uint8_t data)
 		case 1:
 			// Trivial optimization for DAC.
 			if (d->state.OPNAadr == 0x2A) {
-				d->state.DACdata = ((int)data - 0x80) << 7;
+				d->state.DACdata = ((int)data - 0x80) * 128;
 				return 0;
 			}
 
